  "tagline": "Bohu Tang's ANSI C embedded key-value engine for exploring LSM and buffered trees; archived teaching code.",
  "description": "nessDB is an embedded key-value storage engine in ANSI C with no external dependencies, written by Bohu Tang (later a co-founder of Databend) as a vehicle for experimenting with write-optimised indexes. Early versions used an LSM tree, v2 a small-splittable tree, and v3 a buffered (B-epsilon, fractal-style) tree with range queries, compression and simple transactions, behind a Redis-like SET/GET/DEL interface. The author labels it for teaching and research only, and the repository is now archived. It is a compact codebase for studying buffered-tree ideas, not something to deploy.",
